# Round glmcard: GLM-5.3-Flash's routed experts on the A6000 by the expert rule with a hot list, against
# the same binary at a card budget that keeps none. The card experts read Q4_K and Q5_K stacks
# (glm5next::place::card_routed): 39 routed layers take n_l = 67 of 288 each [derived: 40.09 GB after
# the trunk, stores, context, scratch and margin over 39 x 15,204,352 B], and the three with a Q6_K
# down (11, 12, 44) keep every expert on the host, 408.5 MB a token (8 x (18.42 + 16.32 + 16.32 MB)).
# Host bytes a token: 5.152 GB -> 0.408 + 4.744 x (1 - h) GB. Realized list hit h = 43-57 % [derived:
# V4.1's realized decode hit was 1.9x uniform, rig-log 09-24#hot-list-placement-and-real-text-prompt,
# 1.9 x 23.3 % = 44 %; its cross-domain list 46-55 % at 21.5 %, 09-23#v41-router-four-corpora, moved to
# 23.3 %; stage 1's held-out share, docs/cards/glmtrace.card, replaces this before the run]. Saved
# 4.744 h GB = 2.04-2.70 GB at 130-137 GB/s = 14.9-20.8 ms of a 53.6-61.6 ms step (glmhot §0-3)
# [derived]. The card experts run in the host leg's shadow: about 4 experts x 15.2 MB = 61 MB a layer
# at ~600 GB/s, 0.10 ms, plus six launches, under a 0.52-0.55 ms leg, so they add 0 to the wall.
# Gain = step / (step - saved): 61.6 / 46.7 = 1.32 to 53.6 / 32.8 = 1.63.
kind: ab
question: do the card's hot experts shorten GLM's decode step by the host bytes they remove?
term: tg tok/s @ n=96 after prose:512, A6000, plan a, hot list against BLOOMERY_CARD_BUDGET at the
  trunk floor (the CardBudgetFloor error's floor bytes, n_l 0 on every layer), paired by round
unit: %
predict: +32..+63
rounds: 2
condition: one binary, both arms through levers in one lease, a fresh process per arm, the host set
  populated before each timed window (majflt in the window near 0), no [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]
  row; each arm's plan line prints its card_experts (0 on the base arm) and host_experts; the list is
  glm5next-hotlist.txt from the prose set, whose held-out hot-67 share (48.9 %, stage 1) is
  same-document, and exllamav3 #315 measured a hot list drift when only the preceding context changes
  (cold 20.8 -> 28.6 %), so the realized hit on another document may be lower than 48.9 %
decide-in: land glmcard; write the measured host GB/s from the step stats into the GLM cost model
decide-below: read the per-layer leg and the realized card hit from the step stats: a hit under 43 %
  means the list does not transfer to decode; re-derive before any card-side change
decide-above: the fixed per-layer host cost was over-counted: measure the leg per layer before
  opening glmhostfix
